Diagnostic variant "e3" (NOT committed; measured only). Applied on top of
dfc27a0. Replaces the fetch_update in checked_counter_sub with a
compare_exchange_weak loop whose first attempt guesses that the counter
holds exactly `delta`, so the first RMW also fetches the live value with
the cache line held exclusively, instead of a plain load followed by a CAS.
Every write is still a checked value (never wraps, refusal leaves the
counter unchanged). See BENCHMARKS.md, "Issue #214: hot-path recovery".

--- a/src/price_level/level.rs
+++ b/src/price_level/level.rs
@@ pub(crate) fn checked_counter_sub(counter: &AtomicU64, delta: u64) -> bool {
     if delta == 0 {
         return true;
     }
-    counter
-        .fetch_update(Ordering::Relaxed, Ordering::Relaxed, |c| {
-            c.checked_sub(delta)
-        })
-        .is_ok()
+    let mut current = delta;
+    loop {
+        let Some(next) = current.checked_sub(delta) else {
+            return false;
+        };
+        match counter.compare_exchange_weak(current, next, Ordering::Relaxed, Ordering::Relaxed) {
+            Ok(_) => return true,
+            Err(actual) => current = actual,
+        }
+    }
 }

Diagnostic variants "e1" / "e2" (NOT committed; they reintroduce an
